{"id":36600549807388,"type":"album","name":"Naturally","artist":"J.J. Cale","year":1971,"weight":19,"info":{"cover":"https://ia600507.us.archive.org/7/items/mbid-1b335bbf-03cd-4d9c-84d5-9b4972385989/mbid-1b335bbf-03cd-4d9c-84d5-9b4972385989-13995326629.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":12,"country":"US","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"prFiYjAbTkw","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/3cpNHI7xhNIosF9WjSk8Zh","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_mTWnEFVR8YZQxfeW0t62pr4C4x3GqnzkA","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/j_j-cale/naturally"},"desc":"Naturally is the debut album by J. J. Cale. First released in 1972, it includes his song “After Midnight” which was first recorded by Eric Clapton in 1970. Cale, who was languishing in obscurity at the time, had no knowledge of Clapton’s recording of “After Midnight” until it became a radio hit in 1970. Cale’s friend and producer, Audie Ashworth, encouraged Cale to record a full album in order to capitalize on the success of his song. Naturally was recorded independently, “on spec”, the musicians being paid demo fees. Some songs, such as “Call Me the Breeze”, were recorded with ."},"artist_ref":{"id":260620545057301,"name":"J.J. Cale","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/J.J._CALE_%28cropped%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":194427380844280,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":621,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":163225726165579,"type":"genre","name":"Blues Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":458,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":202159817309393,"type":"genre","name":"blues","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":444,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":90510611927654,"type":"genre","name":"Country Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":425,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":33310639067833,"type":"genre","name":"Northern American Music","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":200,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":1